  "id": "gr-mitai",
  "connector": "〜みたい",
  "gloss": "seems; apparently",
  "title": "〜みたい・〜らしい — it seems, apparently",
  "pattern": "plain form (noun / な-adjective without だ) + みたい(だ) / らしい",
  "explanation": "みたい says something seems to be so, from what you see or hear: {彼|かれ}、{疲|つか}れてるみたい — he seems tired. らしい leans on what you’ve heard: あの{店|みせ}、{有名|ゆうめい}らしいよ — apparently that place is famous. みたい also means “like”: {夢|ゆめ}みたい — like a dream.",
  "natural": "みたい is the everyday, casual one; ようです is its polite, written twin.",
  "stiff": "Not about your own feelings, which you know: {私|わたし}は{疲|つか}れたみたい sounds odd. Just {疲|つか}れた.",
